^TBD(230,"K0E6.0186A2")="Use this entity type to create value types that can be assigned to attributes using `sys.attr.range` @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.018708")="Used wherever a value must point to a callable function, such as entvalidfn or validfn attributes @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.01870F")="Used wherever a value can be translatable in multiple languages @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.018716")="Used for compact spatial representation, spatial indexing, proximity search, and geographic partitioning. @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.01871D")="Used wherever a geographic position is represented using the conventional GPS notation of latitude followed by longitude. Unlike WKT POINT, which uses longitude followed by latitude, GPS values follow the human and device-oriented coordinate order (latitude, longitude). @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.018724")="Use this entity type to create attributes that can be assigned to entities @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.01872B")="Use this attribute on an entity being asserted to check required attributes present and entity predicates during staging time. The value must reference the key of a spec entity. @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.018735")="Use this when you need to validate an entity with a number of required attributes. Attach sys.attr.entattribute to a spec entity @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.01873D")="Use this when you need to validate an entity using a set of predicate functions. Attach sys.attr.entvalidationfn to a spec entity @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.01874B")="Use this for well-known abbreviations only, not arbitrary aliases. For alternative names use sys.attr.alias instead. @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.01875B")="Use this to constrain the values of an attribute to a specific value type. Do not confuse range of an attribute with the domain of an attribute. @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.01876A")="Attribute is not descriptive of what the entity is, but prescriptive about how it should be used @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.018770")="It is a multi-value attribute with language tagged directly in the capitalized value using @<lang> syntax @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.01878D")="It is used as the base from which synthetic fully-qualified names are derived across namespaces and types @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.018793")="It is a single-value plain string attribute, not language tagged, intended for generic display purposes such as coordinate summaries or composite value previews @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.01879F")="When you use an example, start with the prefix `e.g.` @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.0187AE")="Atomic multi-value attribute that is used to reference Wikipedia pages related to an object. @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.0187B5")="Atomic single-value attribute used to link an object to its primary official website on the internet. @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.0187C1")="Use this attribute to identify the target entity in every Assert or Retract record. Supply a raw EID (120 characters). @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.0187C8")="Use this attribute to resolve the target entity in every Assert or Retract record. Supply the attribute key of a UNQINSERT/UNQUPSERT attribute.  @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.0187CF")="Use this attribute alongside sys.attr.range when the range is a reference type, to further restrict which entity type the reference must point to. @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.0187D6")="Use notes for supplemental information, implementation details, caveats, historical context, or miscellaneous remarks @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.0187DD")="Notice that each entity belongs to only one entity type. Use an object to capture the multi-type nature of an entity @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.0187E3")="Use this entity type to create enumerated value types whose instances are the allowed constants. Do not use sys.type.val for enumerated types — use sys.type.enum instead. @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.018811")="Use this entity type to create composite value types when a value has multiple interrelated fields (e.g. a magnitude and a unit, or a value and a date) that must be captured together rather than as separate independent attributes. @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.018819")="Use this CVT type to represent a geographic position as a structured value with related spatial components that must be captured together rather than as independent attributes. @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.018821")="Use this entity type to create other fundamental entity types that are necessary for HermesBase to function @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.018827")="Use this type to create association types for people, places, organizations, movies, and more. Use `sys.type.val` to create data types, Use `sys.type.enum` for enumerated types. @en"
^TBD(230,"K0E6.01882D")="Associations are linked to an object with the `object` attribute. @en"
